5"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":true,"disambiguationNote":"Abdon (Hebrew: עַבְדּוֹן ‘Aḇdōn, \"servile\" or \"service\"), was the son of Hillel, a Pirathonite, and was the twelfth Judge of Israel mentioned in the Book of Judges (Judges 12:13-15). He was a member of the tribe of Ephraim, and in the biblical account was credited with having forty sons and thirty grandsons. He restored order in the central area of Israel \"after the disastrous feud with Jephtha and the Gileadites\".[1] He judged Israel for eight years. He was buried on Ephraimite land, in Pirathon, in the hill-country of the Amalekites.","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:abdon_11","nativeName":"Abdon","name":"Abdon","aliases":[],"unit":"Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"abdon_11","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":10,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["1Chr.8.23"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":true,"disambiguationNote":"","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:abdon_12","nativeName":"Abdon","name":"Abdon","aliases":[],"unit":"Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"abdon_12","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":11,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["1Chr.8.30","1Chr.9.36"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":true,"disambiguationNote":"Abdon (A judge of Israel for eight years (Judg 12:13–15). The son of Hillel the Pirathonite and the father of 40