e refortification of this wall (Neh 3:1). The size of his house indicated his wealth and high socio-economic status (Neh 3:23-21). This places him as someone who lived during the time of Nehemiah. In the year 445 BCE, Eliashib was the high priest when Nehemiah returned to Jerusalem in the 20th year of Artaxerxes I (Nehemiah 1:1, 2:1).[1]","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:eliashib_1094","nativeName":"Eliashib","name":"Eliashib","aliases":[],"unit":"Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"eliashib_1094","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":774,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["1Chr.24.12"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":true,"disambiguationNote":"Eliashib (the twelfth to Jakim)","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:eliashib_1095","nativeName":"Eliashib","name":"Eliashib","aliases":[],"unit":"Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"eliashib_1095","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":775,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["Ezra.10.6"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":true,"disambiguationNote":"Eliashib (Jehohanan )","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:eliashib_1096