Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"gaius_1269","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":941,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["Acts.19.29"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":false,"disambiguationNote":"Soon the whole city was in an uproar. The people seized Gaius and Aristarchus, Paul’s traveling companions from Macedonia, and all of them rushed into the theater together","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:gaius_1270","nativeName":"Gaius (of Derbe)","name":"Gaius","aliases":[],"unit":"Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"gaius_1270","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":942,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["Acts.20.4"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":false,"disambiguationNote":"Gaius (from Derbe).","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:gaius_1271","nativeName":"Gaius","name":"Gaius","aliases":[],"unit":"Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"gaius_1271","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":943,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["Rom.16.23","1Cor.1.14"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":true,"disambiguationNote":"Gaius (Travelling Companion of Paul)","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:gaius_1272","nativeName":"Gaius","name":"Gaius","aliases":[],"unit":"Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"gaius_1272","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":944,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["3John.1.1"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":true,"disambiguationNote":"Gaius (the dear friend of John)","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:galal_1273","nativeName":"Galal","name":"Galal","aliases":[],"unit":"Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"galal_1273","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":945,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["1Chr.9.15"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":true,"disambiguationNote":"Galal ( is an Arabic masculine name, often its meaning is majesty as an attribute of God in the Bible, such as Psalms and Christian hymns, and in the Quran. Many Arabic-speaking Christians or other Christians and Arab or non-Arab Muslims have Jalal as given or family name. Majesty is among other approximate meanings of Jalal, such as dignity, greatness, lordliness, loftiness, and glory to address a royal person like king, lord, emperor and monarch as in current monarchies, formal situations, histories, myths, and legends. When the Arabs spread their language over non-Arabic countries through religions or other ways, \"Jalal\", among other Arabic words, has been added to other language dictionaries of non-Arabic people. In the Bible, and in many Psalms, Verses, and Christian hymns, such as Psalms (29:4), (93:1), (111:3), (145:5), etc.[1], Isaiah (2:10), (26:10), (30:30), etc.[1], and the Great Doxology (Christian Hymn), which are written in Arabic and read in Churches, Jalal has the meaning of majesty. For example: Psalm (93:1):[2] \".اَلرَّبُّ قَدْ مَلَكَ. لَبِسَ الْجَلاَلَ. لَبِسَ الرَّبُّ الْقُدْرَةَ، ائْتَزَرَ بِهَا. أَيْضًا تَثَبَّتَتِ الْمَسْكُونَةُ. لاَ تَتَزَعْزَعُ\" which is in English:\"The Lord reigns, he is robed in majesty;...\".[3] Isaiah (26:10):[4] \".يُرْحَمُ الْمُنَافِقُ وَلاَ يَتَعَلَّمُ الْعَدْلَ. فِي أَرْضِ الاسْتِقَامَةِ يَصْنَعُ شَرًّا وَلاَ يَرَى جَلاَلَ الرَّبِّ\" Great Doxology: \".المجد لله في العلى وعلى الأرض السلام، وفي الناس المسرة. نسبحك نباركك، نسجد لك، نمجدك، نشكرك من أجل عظيم جلال مجدك\")","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:galal_1274","nativeName":"Galal","name":"Galal","aliases":[],"unit":"Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"galal_1274","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":946,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["1Chr.9.16","Neh.11.17"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":true,"disambiguationNote":"Galal (son ofJeduthun)","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":null,"historicalIndividualIndependentlyConfirmed":false,"curatedChronologyNotAdopted":{"birthYear":"","deathYear":"","basis":"Maintainer follows modern Jones chronology; not substituted for received witness clocks."}},{"id":"bible:theographic:gallio_1275","nativeName":"Gallio","name":"Gallio","aliases":[],"unit":"Curated Biblical named-entity/person record","sourceRecordKey":"gallio_1275","sourceRecordOrdinalOneBased":947,"sourceRefs":["theographic:CSV/People.csv"],"verseRefs":["Acts.18.12","Acts.18.14","Acts.18.17"],"genderAsCurated":"Male","ambiguousAsCurated":false,"disambiguationNote":"","generation":null,"absoluteChronology":null,"musicalAssignment":